WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:12.980
okay let's practice using solubility
product constant fluorite or CaF2 is

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:18.150
slightly water soluble and dissolves
according to the following equation so

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.580
we have fluoride solid in equilibrium
with the calcium 2 plus ion and 2

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:30.539
fluoride ions now a saturated fluoride
solution is measured as having a calcium

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:37.890
ion concentration of 2.1 times 10 to the
negative 4 molar so what is the

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:43.559
solubility product for fluorite so
that's all the information we need go

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.900
ahead and give this a try.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.560
so let's put
our equilibrium up top and once again we

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:13.110
know that the calcium ion concentration
is 2.1 times 10 to the negative 4 molar

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:18.119
so what can we do with this information
well we know that fluorite is going to

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:24.540
dissolve to give a calcium ion and to
fluoride ions so if enough fluoride has

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:31.049
dissolved so as to give a calcium ion
concentration of that magnitude then we

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.970
know that the fluoride ion concentration
must be double that because there are

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:41.159
two fluorides that form for every
calcium ion so that means the fluoride

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:46.380
ion concentration must be 4.2 times 10
to the negative 4 molar right that has

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.040
exactly double the calcium ion
concentration so we figured that out

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.979
just by stoichiometry now let's write
our Ksp expression so this is just like

00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:00.780
any other equilibrium expression it
involves only aqueous or gaseous species

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.759
and so that means we're just going to
have the calcium ion concentration times

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:10.020
the fluoride ion concentration squared
and then we don't have to put that over

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.709
any reactants because the reactant is a solid

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:17.609
now we have all the information we need
we have the calcium ion concentration

00:02:17.609 --> 00:02:21.569
and we have the fluoride ion
concentration so we just plug those

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:26.909
numbers in and then we do the arithmetic
and we get a Ksp value of three point

00:02:26.909 --> 00:02:31.579
seven times ten to the negative eleven.

